articles.content_en:
Article 1: An act that violates the provisions of national financial management laws and regulations and absorbs funds from the public (including units and individuals) shall, where it concurrently meets the following four conditions and except as otherwise provided in the Criminal Law, be determined as "illegally absorbing public deposits or absorbing public deposits in a disguised form" as provided for in Article 176 of the Criminal Law:
(1) absorbing funds without permission from the relevant department according to law or by borrowing the form of lawful business operations;
(2) publicly publicizing through the Internet, media, promotional meetings, leaflets, mobile phone messages, or other channels;
(3) promising to repay principal and interest or to give returns in the form of currency, physical objects, equity, or other forms within a certain period; and
(4) absorbing funds from the public, i.e., unspecified members of society.
Where funds are absorbed from specific targets among relatives, friends, or within a unit without public publicity, the act shall not be deemed as illegal absorption or disguised absorption of public deposits.

Article 2: Whoever commits any of the following acts shall, where the conditions provided for in Paragraph 1 of Article 1 of this Interpretation are met, be convicted and punished for the crime of illegally absorbing public deposits in accordance with Article 176 of the Criminal Law:
(1) illegally absorbing funds by means of sale-with-repayment, after-sale leasing, agreed repurchase, or sale of property shares, without genuine real estate sales content or without real estate sales as the main purpose;
(2) illegally absorbing funds by means of transferring forest rights and managing and protecting forests on behalf of others, or other means;
(3) illegally absorbing funds by means of substitute planting (breeding), leased planting (breeding), joint planting (breeding), or other means;
(4) illegally absorbing funds by means of commodity repurchase, consignment for sale, or other means, without genuine content of selling commodities or providing services or without selling commodities or providing services as the main purpose;
(5) illegally absorbing funds by means of falsely transferring equity or issuing fictitious bonds, without genuine content of issuing stocks or bonds;
(6) illegally absorbing funds by means of falsely borrowing overseas funds, issuing fictitious funds, or other means, without genuine content of raising funds;
(7) illegally absorbing funds by means of counterfeiting insurance companies, forging insurance documents, or other means, without genuine content of selling insurance;
(8) illegally absorbing funds by means of online lending, investment as shares, virtual currency transactions, or other means;
(9) illegally absorbing funds by means of entrusted wealth management, financial leasing, or other means;
(10) illegally absorbing funds by means of providing "elderly care services," investing in "elderly care projects," selling "elderly care products," or other means;
(11) illegally absorbing funds by using folk "associations" or "societies" or other organizations; and
(12) other acts of illegally absorbing funds.

Article 7: Whoever, for the purpose of illegal possession, uses fraudulent means to commit any of the acts listed in Article 2 of this Interpretation shall be convicted and punished for the crime of fund-raising fraud in accordance with Article 192 of the Criminal Law.
Where illegal fund-raising is conducted by fraudulent means and any of the following circumstances exists, it may be determined as "for the purpose of illegal possession":
(1) the raised funds are not used for production and business operations, or their use for production and business operations is clearly disproportionate to the scale of the raised funds, resulting in the inability to return the raised funds;
(2) the raised funds are squandered wantonly, resulting in the inability to return the raised funds;
(3) the actor flees with the raised funds;
(4) the raised funds are used for illegal or criminal activities;
(5) the actor withdraws or transfers funds, conceals property, or evades returning the funds;
(6) the actor conceals or destroys accounts, or engages in false bankruptcy or false closure, to evade returning the funds;
(7) the actor refuses to account for the whereabouts of the funds, to evade returning the funds; or
(8) other circumstances under which the purpose of illegal possession may be determined.
The purpose of illegal possession in the crime of fund-raising fraud shall be specifically determined based on the circumstances. Where some of the actor's illegal fund-raising acts have the purpose of illegal possession, the raised funds involved in such acts shall be convicted and punished as the crime of fund-raising fraud; where, in a joint crime of illegal fund-raising, some actors have the purpose of illegal possession and other actors do not have the joint intent or conduct of illegally possessing the raised funds, the actors with the purpose of illegal possession shall be convicted and punished for the crime of fund-raising fraud.

Article 12: Where an advertising operator or advertising publisher, in violation of state regulations, uses advertisements to make false publicity for commodities or services related to illegal fund-raising activities, and any of the following circumstances exists, the offender shall be convicted and punished for the crime of false advertising in accordance with Article 222 of the Criminal Law:
(1) the amount of illegal gains is RMB 100,000 yuan or more;
(2) causing serious harmful consequences or adverse social impact;
(3) having been subjected to administrative penalty two or more times for using advertisements to make false publicity within two years; or
(4) other circumstances of a serious nature.
Where a person knowingly provides advertising or other publicity for others engaged in fund-raising crimes such as fraudulent issuance of securities, illegally absorbing public deposits, unauthorized issuance of stocks, company bonds, or enterprise bonds, fund-raising fraud, or organizing or leading pyramid-selling activities, the person shall be punished as an accomplice to the relevant crime.
